Description
Language: 	English
Notes: 	"Over a 24-hour period, from midnight to midnight, Kyle drew self-portraits of himself every hour on the hour. From these drawings he made relief cuts that were then printed onto paint chips. Each paint chip was picked according to its color name--Dark Hour, Mexican Sun, etc.--so that each color corresponds with the time of day of the drawing printed on it. Once bound into book form these portraits can be viewed individually or used as a flipbook to be quickly viewed in succession creating a portrait of Kyle spanning the length of a full day."--Hot Iron Press web site.
Condition: library markings, in protective enclosure.
